From 96e1354e1f601fe4c317c66b9d37a596dd7ec4b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <ivanverbovoy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:54:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] view, sfduo-control: a new window is not drawn until it is
 where it belongs

A window was mapped at whatever size its client asked for and placed
afterwards - by the dock, a beat later - so it was drawn twice over: its
own size and place first, the panel's second, with the client laying its
contents out again in between, and the dock's own slide carrying the first
frame into the second. Filmed at 60 fps, opening a Settings page: the
window appears at about two thirds of the panel, grows over some ten
frames and reflows twice.

A new toplevel is now held: drawn at zero alpha from its map, and let go -
with the fade it used to get at its map - at the first frame it draws
after all of this has happened:

  - it has been put on a panel (phoc_view_tile says so),
  - it is drawn at that panel's size, scale and all: a window wider than a
    panel is scaled down to fit, and the panel is shorter while the shell's
    bar is still on it, so "the size that was asked for" is not enough,
  - and its client has stopped drawing for 110 ms, because a client answers
    the size first and lays its contents out over the frames after.

Whatever is still unsettled after 700 ms is shown anyway, which is also
what a window nobody ever places gets.

Two things had to stop moving for this to be worth anything. A window
still held is tiled without the sliding ghost - what would travel is the
frame it drew before anything placed it, growing into the panel, which is
exactly the motion being removed. And a window put away over another one -
the port's Settings over its own list - fades where it stands instead of
shrinking towards the bottom edge: what the eye follows there is the
window underneath, and a copy of this one flying down over it is one
motion too many.
---
 src/sfduo-control.c | 238 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/sfduo-control.h |   6 +-
 src/view.c          |  53 +++++++---
 3 files changed, 254 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

